*.key
*.pem
*.wasm
.env
node_modules/
pkg/
target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed. Vendoring without a lockfile is incoherent: the point is a build that is
# reproducible offline, and the lockfile is what pins it.

# THE VENDORED TREE IS COMMITTED WHOLE and must not be filtered by the patterns above. Cargo verifies
# every vendored file against .cargo-checksum.json, so one file missed by a pattern breaks the build
# on a fresh clone and presents as corruption rather than as a gitignore rule.
# Measured 2026-09-23: without this line git would add 5354 of 5451 files, excluding 14 .pem and 1 .key.
!vendor/**

# Installer build artifacts: the exe is cross-compiled and the MSI is produced from it, so neither
# belongs in git. installer/build.ps1 documents how to make both.
installer/payload/
installer/*.msi
installer/*.wixpdb

# The browser client is committed: it is embedded into the binary with include_bytes!, so the
# single-MSI deployment has nothing to misplace. The *.wasm rule above must not catch it.
!web/**
